  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 351 AM EST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nAll in all, the long term period (Tuesday Night through the weekend) \nshould be largely uneventful for North and Central Georgia. Strong \nhigh pressure builds and extends south into the TN Valley/Southeast \nstates with amplified mid-level ridging building and being the \nprimary driver of the weather pattern for the area. The net effects \nof high pressure and ridging aloft will keep us mostly dry with \ntemperatures trending warmer each day. Low temperatures are forecast \nto climb back above freezing with values mainly in the 40s to low \n50s (slightly cooler in the 30s). Daytime temperatures will rise \ninto the 60s to low 70s on Wednesday then climbing into the 70s \nessentially areawide Thursday through the weekend.",
